{"content":[{"c":["SYROPHOENICIA*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Homeland of the Greek woman who approached Jesus in the region of Tyre and Sidon and pleaded with him to cast a demon out of her daughter (",{"href":"?bref=Mark.7.26","r":"Mark.7.26","rawR":"Mark.7.26","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Mark.7.26","value":"Mark.7.26"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mk 7:26"},"). The region of Phoenicia was located in the Roman province of Syria. Perhaps the designation of Syrophoenicia was used so as not to confuse this woman’s country with the Phoenicia of North Africa called Libyphoenicia. In a parallel passage, this woman is identified as a Canaanite, a name by which Phoenicians called themselves (",{"href":"?bref=Matt.15.22","r":"Matt.15.22","rawR":"Matt.15.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Matt.15.22","value":"Matt.15.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Mt 15:22"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Syrophoenicia","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Mk 7:26","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Mark.7.26","rawQueryValue":"Mark.7.26","sourceRefExact":"Mark.7.26"},{"anchorText":"Mt 15:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Matt.15.22","rawQueryValue":"Matt.15.22","sourceRefExact":"Matt.15.22"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6bce35878541ff851ef71d4ab350c2efdaf6d3f54304d68a7dd1d1e1bdd5a4d9","sourceItemName":"Syrophoenicia","sourceItemOrder":610,"sourceMember":"Articles/S.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Syrophoenicia","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Syrophoenicia*","title":"Syrophoenicia*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}